hadiths[281]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21083","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Simak, that he heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: before the Hour there are liars."
"21084","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Simak, that he heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: Maiz ibn Malik was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a short man in his waist-wrapper with no cloak upon him. He said: and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was reclining on a cushion on his left. Then he spoke to him, and I do not know what he spoke to him, and I was far from him, between me and him were people. Then he said: take him away. Then he said: return him. Then he spoke to him while I was listening, and he said: take him away and stone him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood as a preacher, while I was listening. He said: then he said: whenever we go out in the way of Allah, one of them stays behind, bleating like the bleating of a goat, granting one of them a heap of milk. By Allah, I cannot get hold of one of them except that I make an example of him."
"21085","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil informed us, he said: Simak informed me, that he heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: the caller to prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would call the adhan, then wait, and would not establish prayer until, when he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come out, he established the prayer when he saw him."
"21086","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Muhajir ibn Mismar, from Amir ibn Sad, he said: I asked Jabir ibn Samurah about the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: religion will remain standing until there are twelve caliphs of Quraysh."
"21087","Then liars will come before the Hour."
"21088","Then a group of Muslims will come out and extract the treasure of the white, Kisra and the family of Kisra."
"21089","And when Allah, blessed and exalted is He, gives one of you good, let him begin with himself and his family."
"21090","And I am your forerunner at the Pond."
"21091","Yazid narrated to us, Misar informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Qibtiyyah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: when we prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we would say: peace be upon you, with our hands, right and left. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: what is with people who throw their hands as if they are the tails of wild horses? Should not one of you be still and point with his hand upon his thigh, then greet his companion on his right and on his left?"
"21092","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Simak, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah, and he was asked about the gray hair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: there were hairs in his head, when he oiled his head they did not show, and when he did not oil it they showed."
"21093","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, Jabir heard say: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Zuhr: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and similar to it, and in Fajr longer than that."
"21094","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Sharik, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten."
"21095","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I said to Jabir ibn Samurah: did you sit with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: yes, he was long in silence, little in laughter. And his companions would mention poetry and things of their affairs in his presence, and they would laugh, and perhaps he smiled."
"21096","Abdullah ibn al-Walid and Muammal narrated to us, the meaning, and this is the wording of Abdullah, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): shall I perform ablution from the meat of sheep? He said: no. He said: shall I pray in the resting place of sheep? He said: yes. He said: shall I perform ablution from the meat of camels? He said: yes. He said: shall I pray in their kneeling places? He said: no."
"21097","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of dark-mixed eyes with little flesh on the heels."
"21098","Umar ibn Sad Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach standing, and sit between the two sermons, and recite verses, and remind the people."
"21099","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, from Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwai, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in the Farewell Pilgrimage: this religion will remain manifest over whoever opposes it, no opponent or dissenter will harm it, until twelve caliphs of my nation pass. He said: then he spoke something I did not understand, so I said to my father: what did he say? He said: all of them are of Quraysh."
"21100","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that a household at al-Harrah were needy. He said: then a she-camel of theirs, or of others, died with them, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted them to eat it. He said: then it sufficed them for the rest of their winter, or their year."
"21101","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Isra'il informed us, from Simak, that he heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: A man died at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has died. He said: He has not died. Then he came to him a second time, then a third time, and informed him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: How did he die? He said: He cut his own throat with a broad arrowhead. He said: So he did not pray over him."
"21102","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, from Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwa'i: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in the Farewell Pilgrimage: This religion will remain dominant over whoever opposes it; neither opponent nor dissenter will harm it, until there pass from my ummah twelve amirs, all of them - then part of the speech of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was hidden from me. My father was closer to the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than me, so I said: O my father, what is it that was hidden from me of the speech of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He says: All of them are from Quraysh."
"21103","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb: I asked Jabir ibn Samurah: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preach? He said: He used to preach standing, except that he would sit for a sitting, then stand."
"21104","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Indeed, before the Hour there will be liars. Simak said: I heard my brother say: Jabir said: So beware of them."
"21105","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, that he asked Jabir ibn Samurah: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do when he prayed Fajr? He said: He would sit in his sitting place until the sun rose."
"21106","Affan narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A company of the Muslims - or of the believers - will conquer the treasure of the family of Kisra which is in the white [palace]."
"21107","He said: And I heard him say: Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, named Madinah Taybah."
"21108","Affan narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there will be liars."
"21109","Affan narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: A mule died - and Hammad ibn Salamah said: a she-camel - belonging to a man, so he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking a ruling, and Jabir ibn Samurah claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to its owner: Do you have nothing that suffices you instead of it? He said: No. He said: Go and eat it. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The correct version is: a she-camel."
"21110","Abd Allah ibn Maymun Abu Abd al-Rahman, meaning al-Raqqi, narrated to us: Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Amr, narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I heard a man ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May I pray in the garment in which I go to my wife? He said: Yes, unless you see something in it, then wash it. This hadith is not raised [to the Prophet] on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr."
"21111","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Ayyub, meaning Ibn Jabir, narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead us in the prescribed prayer, neither lengthening it nor shortening it, moderate in that, and he used to delay al-Atamah [the Isha prayer]."
"21112","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preach standing, so whoever narrates to you that he saw him preach except standing has lied; but sometimes he would come out and see the people few in number, so he would sit, then they would return, then he would stand and preach standing."
"21113","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us: Simak narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I know a stone in Makkah that used to greet me before I was sent; indeed I know it now."
"21114","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us - and I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad - he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to delay the last Isha prayer."
"21115","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us - and I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad -: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Muhajir ibn Mismar, from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas: I wrote to Jabir ibn Samurah with my servant: Inform me of something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he wrote to me: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a Friday, on the evening of the stoning of al-Aslami, say: Religion will remain standing until the Hour comes, or there are over you twelve khalifahs, all of them from Quraysh."
"21116","And I heard him say: A band of the Muslims will conquer the White House, the house of Kisra and the family of Kisra."
"21117","And I heard him say: Indeed, before the Hour there will be liars, so beware of them."
"21118","And I heard him say: When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, gives one of you good, let him begin with himself and his household."
"21119","And I heard him say: I am your predecessor at the Hawd [Basin]."
"21120","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us - and I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad -: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Siyah Abu Yahya, from Imran ibn Rabah, from Ali ibn Umarah, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I was in a gathering in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present, and my father Samurah was sitting in front of me, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed foul speech and affectation of foul speech are not part of Islam, and indeed the best of people in Islam are the best of them in character."
"21121","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us - and I heard it myself from him -: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us: Fitr narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Three things I fear for my ummah: seeking rain by the stars, injustice of the ruler, and denial of divine decree."
"21122","Affan narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preach standing, then sit for a sitting without speaking, then stand and preach another sermon on his minbar; so whoever narrates to you that he saw him preach sitting, do not believe him."
"21123","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us - and Hajjaj [narrated]: Shu'bah informed us - from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over Ibn al-Dahdah - Hajjaj said: over Abu al-Dahdah - then he was brought an unsaddled horse, and a man restrained it, so he rode it and it began to prance with him while we followed him, hastening behind him. A man from the people said: Indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a cluster hanging or lowered in Paradise belongs to Abu al-Dahdah. Hajjaj said in his hadith: A man with us, in the gathering with Jabir ibn Samurah, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a lowered cluster in Paradise belongs to Abu al-Dahdah."
"21124","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I saw a seal on the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the egg of a dove."
"21125","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be twelve amirs. Then he said a word I did not hear, and the people said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"21126","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Does not one of you fear, when he raises his head while in prayer, that his sight will not return to him?"
"21127","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Simak narrated to us: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Islam will remain mighty until twelve khalifahs. Then he said a light word I did not understand. I said to my father: What did he say? He said: He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"21128","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there will be liars."
"21129","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: There was in the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) no white hair except a few hairs in the parting of his head; when he oiled, the oil concealed them."
"21130","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, from Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwa'i: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in the Farewell Pilgrimage: This religion will remain dominant over whoever opposes it; neither opponent nor dissenter will harm it, until there pass from my ummah twelve amirs, all of them from Quraysh. Then the speech of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became hidden from me. My father was closer to the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than me, so I said: O my father, what is it that was hidden from me of the speech of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He says: All of them are from Quraysh. And I testify to my father making me understand: He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"21131","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us: Jabir ibn Samurah informed me that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preach standing on the minbar, then sit, then stand and preach standing. Jabir said to me: Whoever informs you that he used to preach sitting has lied; for by Allah, I prayed with him more than two thousand prayers."
"21132","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us: I asked Jabir about the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: He used to lighten it, and he did not pray the prayer of these people. And he informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Fajr: Qaf and the Glorious Qur'an, and the like of it."
"21133","Abu Kamil and Abu al-Nadr said: Zuhayr narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us: I asked Jabir ibn Samurah: Did you sit with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, often. He would not rise from his prayer place in which he prayed Fajr until the sun rose; when the sun rose he stood. And he was mostly silent - Abu al-Nadr said: mostly silent - and they would talk, taking up matters of Jahiliyyah, and they would laugh, and he would smile."
"21134","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr, he would sit in his prayer place until the sun rose. And he would recite in the Fajr prayer: Qaf and the Glorious Qur'an, and his prayer after that was light."
"21135","Husayn narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach on Friday standing; so whoever narrates to you that he sat, declare him a liar."
"21136","He said: And Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach two sermons: he would preach, then sit, then stand and preach; and the sermon of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his prayer were moderate."
"21137","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the two Eids more than once or twice, without adhan and without iqamah."
"21138","Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ru'asi narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed that a man had killed himself, so he said: Then I will not pray over him."
"21139","Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: Bilal used to call the adhan when the sun declined, without delaying, then he would not call the iqamah until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out; when he came out, he would call the iqamah when he saw him."
"21140","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb: Jabir ibn Samurah informed me: The mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would call the adhan, then wait and not call the iqamah until, when he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come out, he would call the iqamah when he saw him."
"21141","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us: Jabir ibn Samurah informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach on the minbar standing, then sit, then stand and preach standing; so whoever informs you that he used to preach sitting has lied; for by Allah, I prayed with him more than two thousand prayers."
"21142","Hashim narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Simak narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah: Bilal used to call the adhan when the sun had passed its zenith, then he would not call the iqamah until he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he saw him, he would call the iqamah when he saw him."
"21143","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than one hundred times in the mosque while his Companions recalled poetry and matters of Jahiliyyah, and sometimes he would smile with them."
"21144","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: Ma'iz came and confessed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) four times, so he ordered that he be stoned."
"21145","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: When we came to him - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - one of us would sit where he reached."
"21146","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"21147","And he said: No adhan was called for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the two Eids."
"21148","And a man killed himself, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over him."
"21149","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah - raised [to the Prophet]: This religion will remain standing, a company fighting for it, until the Hour comes. Sharik said: I heard it from his brother Ibrahim ibn Harb. I said to Sharik: From whom did he mention it to you all? He said: From Jabir ibn Samurah."
"21150","Hashim narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Khaythamah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Sa'id al-Hamdani, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be after me twelve khalifahs, all of them from Quraysh. Then he returned to his house, and Quraysh came to him and said: Then what will happen? He said: Then there will be turmoil."
"21151","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Simak narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told of a man who slaughtered himself with arrowheads, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then I will not pray over him."
"21152","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us: Jabir informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be after me twelve amirs. Then I did not know what he said after that, so I asked the people, all of them, and they said: He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"21153","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Simak narrated to us: Jabir ibn Samurah informed me that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed, before the Hour there will be liars. So I said: Did you hear it? He said: I heard it."
"21154","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: A man killed himself, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over him."
"21155","Abu Sa'id narrated to us: Za'idah narrated to us: Simak narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preach on Friday except standing; so whoever narrates to you that he sat, declare him a liar, for he did not do it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach, then sit, then stand and preach; he used to preach two sermons, sitting between them, on Friday."
"21156","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: There was in the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) no white hair except a few hairs in the parting of his head; when he oiled, the oil concealed them."
"21157","Bahz and Affan said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned Ma'iz ibn Malik, and he did not mention flogging."
"21158","Bahz and Abu Kamil said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us - Abu Kamil said: Simak informed us - from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach standing."
"21159","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ja'far ibn Abi Thawr ibn Jabir ibn Samurah, from his grandfather, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Should I perform ablution from mutton? He said: If you wish, do so, and if you wish, do not. He said: Should I perform ablution from camel meat? He said: Yes. Then he stopped and returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, may I pray in the resting places of sheep? He said: Yes. He said: May I pray in the resting places of camels? He said: No."
"21160","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gesture with his two fingers and say: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like this one from this one."
"21161","Ibrahim ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Kisra perishes, there will be no Kisra after him, and when Qaysar perishes, there will be no Qaysar after him; and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, their treasures will be spent in the cause of Allah, Blessed and Exalted."
"21162","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be twelve amirs. Then he said a word I did not hear. My father said: Indeed he said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"21163","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preach on Friday except while standing; so whoever narrates to you that he saw him preach while sitting has lied."
"21164","He said: And Simak said: Jabir ibn Samurah said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his sermon were moderate."
"21165","And Jabir ibn Samurah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach standing, then sit, then stand and preach."
"21166","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman: I heard al-Musayyab ibn Rafi' narrate, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he came out to his Companions and said: What is wrong with me that I see you in separate groups, while sitting?"
"21167","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman: I heard al-Musayyab ibn Rafi' narrate, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he entered the mosque and saw people who had raised their hands, so he said: They have raised them as though they are the tails of wild horses; be still in prayer."
"21168","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman: I heard al-Musayyab ibn Rafi' narrate, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Does not one of you fear, when he raises his gaze while in prayer, that his sight will not return to him?"
"21169","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abu Thawr ibn Ikrimah, from his grandfather - and he is Jabir ibn Samurah - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about praying in the resting places of camels, and he said: Do not pray. And he was asked about praying in the folds of sheep, and he said: Pray. And he was asked about ablution from camel meat, and he said: Perform ablution from it. And he was asked about mutton, and he said: If you wish, perform ablution, and if you wish, do not perform ablution."
"21170","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Simak ibn Harb: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sit between the two sermons on Friday, and preach standing; and his prayer was moderate and his sermon was moderate, and he would recite verses of the Qur'an on the minbar."
"21171","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Dawud narrated to us, from Amir: Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwa'i narrated to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: Indeed this religion will remain mighty until twelve khalifahs. Then he spoke a word I did not understand, and the people clamored, so I said to my father: What did he say? He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"21172","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us: Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at Arafat and said: This matter will remain mighty, protected, dominant over whoever opposes it, until twelve rule, all of them - then I did not understand what came after. So I said to my father: What did he say after he said: all of them? He said: All of them are from Quraysh. And from the hadith of Abu Abd al-Rahman, from his shaykhs, from the hadith of Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21173","Abd Allah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Warkani narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, meaning Ibn Samurah: I sat with him more than one hundred times - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - thus al-Warkani said: He would preach only standing: he would preach his first sermon, then sit for a sitting, then stand and preach his other sermon."
"21174","Abd Allah narrated to us: Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us: Sallam Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to delay Isha."
"21175","Abd Allah narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: A man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wounded, and the wound pained him, so he dragged himself to arrowheads and slaughtered himself with them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over him. And he said: All of that was discipline from him. Thus Abd Allah ibn Amir dictated it to us from his book, and I do not think this addition is except from the speech of Sharik - his saying: that was discipline from him."
"21176","Abd Allah narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman al-Mu'allim Abu Muslim narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Jabir al-Yamami narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah: A Jurmuqani man came to the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Where is this companion of yours who claims he is a prophet? If I ask him, I will surely know whether he is a prophet or not a prophet. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, so the Jurmuqani said: Recite to me, or narrate to me. So he recited to him verses from the Book of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and the Jurmuqani said: This, by Allah, is that which Musa came with, peace be upon him. Abd Allah ibn Ahmad said: This hadith is munkar [rejected]."
"21177","Abd Allah narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim Abu Ali al-Mawsili narrated to me: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his prayer was moderate and his sermon was moderate."
"21178","With this chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two sermons, sitting between them, reciting the Qur'an and reminding the people."
"21179","He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, named Madinah Tabah."
"21180","Abd Allah narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: Whenever food was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would take some of it, then send its remainder to Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him. So food containing garlic was gifted to him, and he sent it to Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, without taking anything from it. Abu Ayyub did not see the trace of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the food, so he brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about that. He said: I only left it because of its smell. Abu Ayyub said: And I dislike what you dislike."
"21181","He narrated to us. [Source text truncated to this single word in the Arabic index.]"
"21182","He narrated to us. [Source text truncated to this single word in the Arabic index.]"
"21183","He narrated to us. [Source text truncated to this single word in the Arabic index.]"
"21184","He narrated to us. [Source text truncated to this single word in the Arabic index.]"
"21185","He narrated to us. [Source text truncated to this single word in the Arabic index.]"
