"21196","Abd Allah narrated to us: Abu Sulayman al-Dabbi Dawud ibn Amr al-Musayyabi narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I prayed with him the two Eids, and no adhan was called for him and no iqamah."
"21197","Abd Allah narrated to us: Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to delay Isha."
"21198","Abd Allah narrated to us: Khallad ibn Aslam Abu Bakr narrated to us: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there will be liars. And Simak said: And my brother said to me: Indeed he said: So beware of them."
"21199","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I know a stone in Makkah that used to greet me before I was sent; indeed I know it now."
"21200","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us - and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah informed us - from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over Ibn al-Dahdah - Hajjaj said: Abu al-Dahdah - then he was brought a bare horse, and a man restrained it, so he rode it and it began to prance with him while we followed him, hastening behind him. A man from the people said: Indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a hanging cluster, or lowered, in Paradise belongs to Abu al-Dahdah. Hajjaj said in his hadith: A man with us, in the gathering with Jabir ibn Samurah, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a lowered cluster in Paradise belongs to Abu al-Dahdah."
"21201","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I saw a seal on the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as if it were a dove's egg."
"21202","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be twelve rulers, then he said a word I did not hear, then the people said: all of them from Quraysh."
"21203","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Said ibn Amir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, meaning Ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whenever he ate food would send its remainder to Abu Ayyub, so he sent to him a remainder from which he had not eaten, containing garlic, so Abu Ayyub came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, is it unlawful, he said: No, but I disliked it because of its smell, so Abu Ayyub said: Then I dislike what you disliked."
"21204","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Naji narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whenever food was brought to him and he ate from it, he would send its remainder to Abu Ayyub, and Abu Ayyub would follow the traces of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), placing his fingers where he saw the trace of his fingers, then one day a large dish was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he found in it the smell of garlic, so he did not taste it and sent it to Abu Ayyub, who did not see the trace of the fingers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not see in it the trace of your fingers, he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I found in it the smell of garlic, he said: Why do you send to me what you do not eat, so he said: The angel comes to me."
"21205","Abdullah narrated to us, Shayban ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: They used to say Yathrib and al-Madinah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, named it Taybah."
"21206","Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated from Nasih Abu Abdullah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For a man to discipline his child, or one of you to discipline his child, is better for him than to give charity every day with half a sa. Abdullah said: And this hadith my father did not include in his Musnad because of Nasih, for he is weak in hadith, and he dictated it to me among the addenda."
"21207","Abdullah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yahya ibn al-Rabi, and he is Ibn Abi al-Rabi al-Jurjani, narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned Maiz and did not mention flogging."
"21208","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Said narrated to me, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there will be liars."
"21209","Abdullah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that a man was with his father at al-Harrah, and a man said to him: A she-camel of mine has gone missing, so if you find it then hold it, so the man found it, and its owner did not come until it fell ill, so his wife said to him: Slaughter it so we may eat it, but he did not do so until it died, so his wife said: Skin it so we may cut its meat and fat into strips, he said: Until I ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he asked him, and he said: Do you have anything that suffices you instead of it, he said: No, he said: Eat it, then its owner came afterwards and said to him: Why did you not slaughter it, he said: I was shy before you."
"21210","Abdullah narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Said narrated to me, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over a man who killed himself."
"21211","Abdullah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar al-Muqri narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at Arafah and said: This religion will remain mighty, protected, triumphant over whoever opposes it, not harmed by whoever leaves it or opposes it, until twelve rule, all of them from Quraysh, or as he said."
"21212","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at Arafat and said: This affair will remain mighty, protected, triumphant over whoever opposes it, until twelve rule, all of them, he said: Then I did not understand what came after, he said: So I said to my father: What is after all of them, he said: All of them from Quraysh."
"21213","Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Sharik ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, and Ibn Abi Layla from Nafi from Ibn Umar, they said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"21214","Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Sharik ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, and Ibn Abi Layla from Nafi from Ibn Umar, they said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"21215","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, I think from Ashath, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to fast Ashura and urge us upon it and check upon us regarding it, then when Ramadan was made obligatory, he neither commanded us nor forbade us regarding it, nor checked upon us regarding it."
"21216","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from al-Ashath, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to perform ablution from camel meat and not to perform ablution from sheep meat, and to pray in sheep folds and not to pray in camel resting places."
"21217","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to me, Ishaq, meaning Ibn Mansur al-Saluli, narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that a man cut his own throat with a broad arrowhead, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over him."
"21218","Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him reclining on his elbow."
"21219","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Amr al-Anbari Ubaydullah ibn Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to me, my father narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I asked Jabir ibn Samurah about the description of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: He had large eyes, a wide mouth, and lean heels."
"21220","Abdullah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar al-Muqri narrated to me, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr, he would sit in his place of prayer until the sun rose."
"21221","Abdullah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman, meaning this hadith, and the hadith of Khalaf from Sharik does not contain Simak in it, rather Khalaf heard it, and Allah knows best, from al-Mubaraki from Sharik, that it was not in his book from Simak."
"21222","Abdullah narrated to us, Khalaf also narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Muhammad al-Mubaraki narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"21223","Abdullah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, named al-Madinah Tabah."
"21224","Abdullah narrated to us, Shuja ibn Makhlad Abu al-Fadl narrated to me, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Simak, he is Ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The shanks of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were slender, and he would not laugh except smiling, and whenever I saw him I would say: He has kohl-lined eyes, though he did not have kohl."
"21225","Abdullah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to me, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: A mule died belonging to a man, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking for a ruling, he said: So Jabir ibn Samurah claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to its owner: What is wrong with you, what suffices you instead of it, he said: No, he said: Then go and eat it."
"21226","Abdullah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching standing, sitting for a sitting in which he did not speak, then standing and preaching another sermon standing, so whoever narrates to you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached sitting, do not believe him."
"21227","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Ahmad Makhlad ibn al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Abi Zumayl, narrated to me, Ubaydullah, meaning Ibn Amr al-Raqqi, narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Shall I pray in the garment in which I approach my wife, he said: Yes, unless you see something in it, then wash it."
"21228","Abdullah ibn Maymun Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubaydullah, meaning Ibn Amr, narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I heard a man ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Shall I pray in my garment in which I approach my wife, he said: Yes, unless you see something in it, then wash it."
"21229","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I came with my father to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was saying: This affair will remain sound until there are twelve rulers, then he said a word I did not understand, so I said to my father: What did he say, he said: All of them from Quraysh."
"21230","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This affair will remain in effect until twelve rulers stand, then he spoke a word that was hidden from me, so I asked my father about it, what did he say, he said: All of them from Quraysh."
"21231","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I was with my father at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This religion will remain mighty, or he said: People will remain in good, Abu Abd al-Samad doubted, until twelve caliphs, then he said a hidden word, so I said to my father: What did he say, he said: All of them from Quraysh."
"21232","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to me, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Mawhab, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they asked him: Shall we perform ablution from sheep meat, so he said: If you wish, perform ablution, and if you wish, do not perform ablution, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we perform ablution from camel meat, he said: Yes, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we pray in sheep resting places, he said: Yes, they said: Shall we pray in camel resting places, he said: No."
"21233","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Abu Awn narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: This affair will remain mighty, protected, they will be aided over whoever opposes them in it, until twelve caliphs, then he said a word the people deafened me from, so I said to my father: What did he say, he said: All of them from Quraysh."
"21234","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Zuhayr ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Amir, meaning al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This affair will remain mighty until twelve caliphs, so the people exclaimed Allahu Akbar and clamored, and he said a hidden word, I said to my father: O my father, what did he say, he said: All of them from Quraysh."
"21235","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sit between the two sermons on Friday, and preach standing, and his prayer was moderate and his sermon was moderate, and he would recite verses from the Quran upon the pulpit."
"21236","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Habib Luwayn narrated to me, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: When we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), each of us would sit where he reached."
"21237","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ghalib narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten of Ramadan, in the odd nights, for I had seen it then I was made to forget it; it is a night of rain and wind, or he said: drizzle and wind."
"21238","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ghalib narrated to us, Amr, and he is Ibn Talhah, narrated to us, Asbat narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: Al-Madinah was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, named al-Madinah Tabah. Jabir said: And I was listening to him."
"21239","And with the same chain, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prayed behind him on a day of Eid without adhan and without iqamah, and Simak claimed that he prayed behind al-Numan ibn Bashir and al-Mughirah ibn Shubah without adhan and without iqamah."
"21240","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to me, Amr narrated to us, Asbat narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from one who narrated to him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: This religion will remain established, a band of Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour comes."
"21241","Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to me, in the year two hundred and twenty-nine, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I saw the seal between the shoulders of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as if it were an egg."
"21242","Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah narrated to me, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, that he heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the funeral of Abu al-Dahdah, while he was upon a horse that was prancing, and we were hastening around him."
"21243","Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah narrated to me, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: Maiz ibn Malik came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have committed adultery, so he turned him away twice, then he stoned him."
"21244","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani Sulayman ibn Dawud, and Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri, and Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Mujalid ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at Arafat, and al-Muqaddami said in his hadith: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching at Mina, and this is the wording of the hadith of Abu al-Rabi, so I heard him say: This affair will remain mighty, triumphant, until twelve rule, all of them, then the people clamored and spoke, so I did not understand his saying after all of them, so I said to my father: O my father, what is after all of them, he said: All of them from Quraysh, and al-Qawariri said in his hadith: Not harmed by whoever opposes him or leaves him, until twelve rule."
"21245","Abdullah narrated to us, Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to me, my father narrated to me, Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, from Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwai, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage say: This religion will remain triumphant over all who oppose it, and not harmed by whoever opposes him or leaves him."
"21246","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated to me, Sulaym ibn Akhdar narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from al-Shabi, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This religion will remain mighty, protected, they will be aided over whoever opposes them in it, until twelve caliphs, he said: So the people began standing and sitting."
"21247","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When Caesar perishes there will be no Caesar after him, and when Khosrau perishes there will be no Khosrau after him, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, their treasures will surely be spent in the cause of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He."
"21248","Abdullah narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me, from Umar ibn Ubayd, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be after me twelve rulers, then speech was made and it was hidden from me, so I asked the one next to me, or beside me, and he said: All of them from Quraysh."
"21249","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Ibrahim al-Tarjuman, he is Ismail ibn Ibrahim, narrated to me, Abu Umar al-Muqri narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of an animal for an animal on credit."
"21250","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to me, and Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to me, and Yusuf al-Saffar, freedman of Banu Umayyah, they said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Siyah al-Thaqafi, Imran ibn Muslim ibn Riyah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Umarah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I was sitting in a gathering in which was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and my father Samurah was sitting before me, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Obscenity and being obscene are in no way part of Islam, and the best of people in Islam are the best of them in character. Ibn Abi Shaybah said in his hadith: Zakariyya ibn Abi Yahya, from Imran ibn Riyah."
"21251","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu al-Qasim al-Zuhri Abdullah ibn Sad narrated to me, my father and my uncle narrated to us, they said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Umar ibn Musa ibn al-Wajih narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) go out with the funeral of Thabit ibn al-Dahdahah, upon a blaze-faced, white-footed horse beneath him with no saddle upon it, with the people accompanying him, while they were around him, he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted and prayed over him, then sat until it was finished, then stood and mounted his horse, then went forth with the men walking around him."
"21252","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu al-Qasim al-Zuhri narrated to me, my uncle narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: Whoever narrates to you that he ever saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching sitting, do not believe him; I saw him more than a hundred times, and I saw him preach standing, then sit without speaking anything, then stand and preach his other sermon. I said: How was his sermon, he said: It was moderate, speech with which he admonished the people, and he would recite verses from the Book of Allah, Exalted is He."
"21253","Abdullah narrated to us, Imran ibn Bakkar al-Himsi narrated to me, Ahmad, meaning Ibn Khalid al-Wahbi, narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A band of Muslims will surely conquer the white palaces of the family of Khosrau."
"21254","Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Umar ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never seen preaching except standing."
"21255","Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to me, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr, he would sit in his place of prayer, not returning, until the sun rose."
"21256","Abdullah narrated to us, Qasim ibn Dinar narrated to us, Musab, meaning Ibn al-Miqdam, narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in his sermon verses from the Quran and remind the people, and his sermon was moderate and his prayer was moderate."
"21257","Abdullah narrated to us, al-Sanani narrated to me, Salamah ibn Hafs al-Sadi narrated to us, Abdullah said: And I myself saw Salamah ibn Hafs, and he was kunya'd Abu Bakr, from the descendants of Sad ibn Malik, white of head and beard, so Abu Bakr al-Sanani narrated to me from him, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Israil, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The finger of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was prominent."
"21258","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, Jabir ibn Samurah narrated to us, saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Islam will remain mighty until twelve caliphs, then he said a hidden word I did not understand, he said: So I said to my father: What did he say, he said: All of them from Quraysh."
"21259","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there will be liars."
"21260","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: There was no white hair on the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except a few hairs on the parting of his head; when he oiled, the oil concealed them."
"21261","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Samurah informed me that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching standing upon the pulpit, then sitting, then standing and preaching standing, he said: So Jabir said to me: Whoever informs you that he used to preach sitting has lied, for by Allah, I prayed with him more than two thousand prayers."
"21262","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to me, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Abu Thawr ibn Ikrimah ibn Jabir ibn Samurah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about prayer in sheep resting places, so he permitted it, and he was asked about prayer in camel resting places, so he forbade it, and he was asked about ablution from camel meat, so he said: Perform ablution, and he was asked about ablution from sheep meat, so he said: If you wish, perform ablution, and if you wish, then not."
"21263","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man came to him and said: Shall I perform ablution from sheep meat, he said: No, he said: Shall I pray in their resting places, he said: Yes, if you wish, he said: Shall I perform ablution from camel meat, he said: Yes, he said: Shall I pray in their resting places, he said: No."
"21264","He narrated to us."
"21265","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Amash, Musayyab ibn Rafi narrated to me, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque while they were in circles, so he said: What is wrong with me that I see you in separate groups, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque after they had raised their hands, so he said: They have raised them as if they are the tails of restive horses; be still in prayer."
"21266","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, Simak narrated to me, and Ibn Jafar, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Ibn Jafar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there will be liars, Yahya said in his hadith: My father said, and he was closer to me than I, so beware of them."
"21267","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Simak narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would preach on Friday standing, then sit, then stand."
"21268","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Simak narrated to me, he said: I said to Jabir ibn Samurah: How would the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do when he prayed Fajr, he said: He would sit in his place of prayer until the sun rose."
"21269","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwai say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This affair will remain in effect until twelve rulers stand, then he spoke a word hidden from me, so I asked my father, what did he say, he said: All of them from Quraysh."
"21270","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in Zuhr: By the night when it covers, and in Asr similar to that, and in Fajr longer than that."
"21271","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us one day and said: What is wrong with me that I see you raising your hands as if they are the tails of restive horses; be still in prayer."
"21272","Then he came out to us and saw us in circles, so he said: What is wrong with me that I see you in separate groups."
"21273","Then he came out to us and said: Will you not line up as the angels line up before their Lord, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, how do the angels line up before their Lord, he said: They complete the first rows and stand close together in the row."
"21274","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will surely stop raising their gazes to the sky in prayer, or they will not return to them."
"21275","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I was with my father, or my son, he said: And he mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: This affair will remain mighty, protected, they will be aided over whoever opposes them in it, until twelve caliphs, then he spoke a word the people deafened me from, so I said to my father, or to my son: What is the word the people deafened me from, he said: All of them from Quraysh."
"21276","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, Simak narrated to me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour there will be liars, my brother said, and he was closer to him than I: I heard him say: So beware of them."
"21277","Abu Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, Simak, meaning Ibn Harb, narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the morning prayer, he would sit in his place of prayer until the sun rose, bright."
"21278","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, Simak narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, named al-Madinah Tabah."
"21279","Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Nasih Abu Ubaydullah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For a man to discipline his child is better for him than to give charity every day with half a sa. And Abu Abd al-Rahman said: My father narrated to me from Nasih Abu Ubaydullah nothing other than this hadith."
"21280","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Simak, he said: I asked Jabir ibn Samurah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in Fajr: Qaf, by the Glorious Quran, and the like."
"21281","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Ubaydullah Ibn al-Qibtiyyah, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: We would say behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when we gave salam: Peace be upon you, peace be upon you, each of us gesturing with his hand to his right and to his left, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is wrong with those who throw their hands in prayer as if they are the tails of restive horses; is it not enough for one of you to place his hand upon his thigh, then give salam to his right and to his left."
"21282","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would preach standing, and sit between the two sermons, and recite verses from the Quran, and his sermon was moderate and his prayer was moderate."
"21283","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi ibn Sabrah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying in camel resting places, and permitted praying in sheep resting places."
"21284","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from Jafar, meaning Ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to perform ablution from camel meat, and not to perform ablution from sheep meat, and to pray in sheep folds, and not to pray in camel resting places."
"21285","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his house, and I saw him reclining upon a cushion."
"21286","Waki narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a horse when he left the funeral of Abu al-Dahdah, so he rode, while we were around him walking."
"21287","Waki narrated to us, Israil and Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that a man killed himself, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over him."
"21288","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to me, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I saw it like a dove's egg, and its color was the color of his body."
"21289","Waki narrated to us, from al-Masudi, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: Maiz ibn Malik came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and confessed to him adultery, he said: So he turned his face away, he said: Then he came and confessed repeatedly, so he ordered him stoned, so he was stoned, then he was brought and informed, so he stood and praised Allah, Exalted is He, and extolled Him, then said: What is wrong with men, whenever we go forth in the cause of Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, one of them stays behind with them, having braying like the braying of a billy goat, granting one of them a small amount of milk; if Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, enables me over them, I shall surely make them an example."
"21290","Abdullah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or a man said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I perform ablution from sheep meat, he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, then he mentioned the hadith."
"21291","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I heard Hajjaj ibn al-Shair ask my father, saying: Which is more beloved to you, Amr al-Naqid or al-Muayti, so he said: Amr al-Naqid used to seek exact truthfulness."
"21292","Waki narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two."
"21293","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in Zuhr and Asr: By the sky with the constellations, and: By the sky and the night-comer, and the like."
"21294","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: A short, disheveled-haired, muscular man wearing an izar, who had committed adultery, was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he turned him away twice, he said: Then he ordered him stoned, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whenever we go forth raiding in the cause of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, one of you stays behind, having braying like the braying of a billy goat, granting one of them a small amount of milk; Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, will not enable me over any of them except I shall make him an example, or I shall punish him exemplarily, he said: So Said ibn Jubayr narrated it to me, saying: He turned him away four times."
"21295","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Maiz ibn Malik was brought to him, then he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: One of them stays behind, braying like the braying of a billy goat, he said: So I narrated it to al-Hakam, and it pleased him, and he said to me: What is al-kuthbah, so I asked Simak about al-kuthbah, and he said: A small amount of milk."
"21296","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: This religion will remain established, a band of Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour comes."
"21297","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a wide mouth, large eyes, and lean heels. I said to Simak: What is wide-mouthed, he said: Large of mouth, I said: What is large-eyed, he said: Long of eyelash, I said: What is lean-heeled, he said: Scant of flesh of the heel."
"21298","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The white treasures of Khosrau will surely be conquered, Shubah said, or he said: Which is in the white, a band of Muslims."
"21299","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: There was no white hair on the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except a few hairs on the parting of his head; when he oiled, it covered them."
"21300","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in Fajr: Qaf, by the Quran, and his prayer afterwards was light."
"21301","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when food was brought to him he ate from it and sent its remainder to Abu Ayyub, and Abu Ayyub would place his fingers where he saw the trace of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a bowl and he found the smell of garlic from it, so he did not taste it and sent it to Abu Ayyub, and he looked and did not see in it the trace of the fingers of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he did not taste it, then he came to him and said, O Messenger of Allah, I did not see in it the trace of your fingers, he said, I found the smell of garlic from it, he said, So do you send to me what you do not eat, he said, The angel comes to me."
"21302","Abdullah narrated to us, he said, I heard one of our companions saying, from Ali ibn al-Madini, he said, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah said to me, Do you have a hadith better than this and with a better chain than this, he said, I said, What is it, he said, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to me, from his father, from Umm Ayyub, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stayed with Abu Ayyub, then he mentioned this hadith of garlic, he said, I said to him, Yes, Shu'bah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stayed with Abu Ayyub, then he fell silent."
"21303","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Simak informed us, he said, I heard Jabir ibn Samurah, and it was said to him, Was there gray hair on the head of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said, There were only a few hairs on his head and none in his beard except hairs at the parting of his head, when he oiled them the oil concealed them."
"21304","Abu Kamil and Bahz said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, Abu Kamil said, Simak informed us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that a man was at al-Harrah with his family and children, and a man said to him, I have lost a camel of mine, so if you find her then hold her, so he found her and she fell sick, and his wife said to him, Slaughter her, and he refused, then she died, and his wife said to him, Cut her into strips so we may eat from her meat and fat, he said, Until I consult the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he came to him and informed him, and he said to him, Do you have wealth that suffices you, he said, No, he said, Then eat it, he said, Then its owner came after that and said, Why did you not slaughter her, he said, I was shy of you."
"21305","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"21306","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, and Yahya ibn Adam, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, that he heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray the prayers like the prayer of yours which you pray today, but he used to lighten, his prayer was lighter than your prayer, and he used to recite in Fajr al-Waqi'ah and the like of it among the surahs."
"21307","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, and Abu Nu'aym, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, that he heard Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, A group of Muslims will conquer the treasures of Kisra, Abu Nu'aym said, which is at al-Abyad, Jabir said, So I was among them, and I received one thousand dirhams."
"21308","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Simak, that he heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying, The mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would call the adhan then wait, until when he saw the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, come out, he would establish the prayer when he saw him."
"21309","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Simak, that he heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had gray at the front of his head and his beard, so when he oiled and combed it did not show, and when his head was disheveled it showed, and he had abundant hair and beard, and a man said, Was his face like a sword, he said, No, rather it was like the sun and the moon, round, he said, And I saw his seal by his shoulder like a pigeon egg, resembling his body."
"21310","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Simak, that he heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had gray at the front of his head and his beard, so when he oiled and combed it did not show, and when his head was disheveled it showed, and he had abundant hair and beard, and a man said, Was his face like a sword, he said, No, rather it was like the sun and the moon, round, he said, And I saw his seal by his shoulder like a pigeon egg, resembling his body."
"21311","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had become gray, then he mentioned its meaning."
"21312","Abd al-Razzaq and Khalaf ibn al-Walid said, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, that he heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in Fajr prayer, and he began to gesture with his hand, Khalaf said, gesturing in prayer before him, and the people asked him when he finished, and he said, Satan was casting sparks of fire at me to distract me from my prayer, so I seized him, and had I taken him he would not have escaped from me until he was tied to a pillar among the pillars of the mosque, with the children of the people of Madinah looking at him."
"21313","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would call the adhan then wait and would not establish until when he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, come out, he would establish the prayer when he saw him."
"21314","Yahya ibn Hammad and Affan said, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray the prayers like your prayer, and he used to delay the night prayer a little after your prayer, and he used to lighten the prayer."
"21315","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite in Fajr prayer Qaf and the Quran of glory, and his prayer thereafter was light."
"21316","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prayed Fajr, would sit in his prayer place until the sun rose."
"21317","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Abbad, meaning Ibn al-Awwam, narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The shanks of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were slender, and he would not laugh except smiling, and when I looked at him I would say, He is kohl-eyed, though he was not kohl-eyed."
"21318","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Mu'adh al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, In Makkah there is a stone that used to greet me on the nights I was sent, I know it when I pass by it."
"21319","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, he said, I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in Subh prayer, and he began to snatch at something before him, and when he finished we asked him, and he said, That was Satan, he cast sparks of fire at my feet to distract me from prayer, he said, And I snatched at him, and had I taken him he would have been tied to a pillar among the pillars of the mosque until the children of the people of Madinah circled around him."
"21320","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would call the adhan then would not establish, waiting, until when he saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, come out, he would establish the prayer."
"21321","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath, from Ja'far ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to command fasting Ashura and urge us to it and check on us for it, then when Ramadan was made obligatory he did not command us with it nor forbid us from it nor check on us for it."
"21322","Hashim narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath, from Ja'far ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to perform ablution from camel meat and not to perform ablution from sheep meat, and to pray in sheep pens and not to pray in camel resting places."
"21323","Abu Salamah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Simak, from Jabir, he said, We used to sit with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and they would recite poetry to one another and mention things from the affairs of Jahiliyyah, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was silent, and perhaps he smiled, or he said, We would recite poetry and mention things from the affairs of Jahiliyyah, and perhaps he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smiled."
"21324","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri and Khalaf ibn al-Walid said, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, that he heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, This affair will remain standing, the Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour comes, Abu Abd al-Rahman said, This is Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, he is not of the children of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, rather his grandfather's name was al-Zubayr."
"21325","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, When Qaysar is gone there will be no Qaysar after him, and when Kisra is gone there will be no Kisra after him, and by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, their treasures will be spent in the path of Allah, Blessed and Exalted."
"21326","Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, There will be twelve caliphs for this nation."
"21327","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, I was informed that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, This religion will remain standing, a group of Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour comes."
"21328","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, I was sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a man came to him and said, O Messenger of Allah, shall we perform ablution from sheep meat, he said, If you wish perform ablution from it, and if you wish do not perform ablution from it, he said, Shall I perform ablution from camel meat, he said, Yes, perform ablution from camel meat, he said, Shall we pray in camel kneeling places, he said, No, he said, Shall we pray in sheep folds, he said, Yes, pray in sheep folds."
"21329","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray Dhuhr when the sun had declined."
"21330","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, Bilal would call the adhan when the sun had declined."
"21331","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite in Dhuhr and Asr By the heaven and the night comer, and By the heaven of constellations, and the like of them among the surahs."
"21332","Abu Kamil and Bahz said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that Bilal would call the adhan for Dhuhr when the sun had declined."
"21333","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, he said, I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, Islam will remain mighty until twelve caliphs, then he said a hidden word I did not understand, he said, I said to my father, What did he say, he said, All of them are from Quraysh."
"21334","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, he said, I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying, I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, Before the Hour there will be liars."
"21335","Bahz and Surayj said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The people would say Yathrib and al-Madinah, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, named it Tabah, Surayj said, Yathrib is al-Madinah."
"21336","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he ate food would send its remainder to Abu Ayyub, and Abu Ayyub would place his fingers where he saw the fingers of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought food and found in it the smell of garlic, so he did not eat, and sent it to Abu Ayyub, and he did not see in it the trace of the fingers of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said, O Messenger of Allah, I did not see in it the trace of your fingers, he said, I found the smell of garlic from it, he said, Do you send to me what you do not eat, he said, The angel comes to me."
"21337","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Tamim ibn Tarafah al-Ta'i, from Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwa'i, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Will you not line up as the angels line up before their Lord, Blessed and Exalted, he said, We said, O Messenger of Allah, how do the angels line up before their Lord, he said, They complete the first rows and stand close together in the row."
"21338","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The prayer of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was moderate, and his sermon was moderate."
"21339","He narrated to us."
"21340","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon us while we were raising our hands in prayer, and said, Why do I see you raising your hands as if they are the tails of restive horses, be still in prayer."
"21341","He said, And he came upon us in the mosque while we were separate circles, and said, Why do I see you in separate groups."
"21342","Waki' narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Ubaydullah Ibn al-Qibtiyyah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, When we prayed behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one of us would gesture to his brother from on his right and from on his left, then when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed, he said, What is with one of you doing this as if they are the tails of restive horses, it suffices one of you, or does it not suffice one of you, to say thus, and he placed his right hand on his thigh and pointed with his finger, greeting his brother from on his right and from on his left."
"21343","Waki' narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, There was no adhan called for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor iqama for him on the two Eids."
"21344","Waki' narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, and Sharik and Hajjaj, he said, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that a man killed himself, Hajjaj said, at the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not pray over him."
"21345","Waki' narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, I saw it like a pigeon egg, its color the color of his body."
"21346","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would sit in his prayer place when he prayed the morning prayer until the sun rose bright."
"21347","Waki' narrated to us, from Fitr, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, This affair will remain attainable or near until twelve caliphs stand, all of them from Quraysh."
"21348","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to remind in his sermon."
"21349","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would sit between the two sermons and recite verses from the Quran, and his prayer was moderate and his sermon was moderate."
"21350","Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Before the Hour there will be liars."
"21351","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak, he said, I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prayed Subh, would sit in his prayer place until the sun rose bright or the sun rose high and bright."
"21352","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would preach standing and sit then stand, reciting verses and remembering Allah, Exalted, and his sermon was moderate and his prayer was moderate."
"21353","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, I came with my father to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was saying, This affair will remain sound until there are twelve commanders, then he said a word I did not understand, I said to my father, What did he say, he said, He said, All of them are from Quraysh."
"21354","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, When we reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one of us would sit where he ended up."
"21355","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Hammad, and Bahz said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned Ma'iz ibn Malik and did not mention flogging."
"21356","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said, People who raise their eyes to the sky in prayer will stop, or it will not return to them."
"21357","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Mansur, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, I and the Hour were sent like these two."
"21358","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ja'far ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that a man came to him and said, Shall I perform ablution from sheep meat, he said, No, he said, Shall I pray in its folds, he said, Yes if you wish, he said, Shall I perform ablution from camel meat, he said, Yes, he said, Shall I pray in its resting places, he said, No."
"21359","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, I was informed that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, This religion will remain standing, a group of Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour comes."
"21360","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and once he said, I heard Jabir, meaning Ibn Samurah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, named al-Madinah Tabah."
"21361","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, he said, The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would recite in Dhuhr and Asr By the night when it covers and the like of that, and in Subh longer than that."
"21362","Abd al-Rahman and Affan said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would recite in Dhuhr and Asr By the heaven of constellations and By the heaven and the night comer and the like, Affan said, and the like of them among the surahs."
"21363","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said, I heard Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, Allah, Exalted, named al-Madinah Tabah."
